On the embedding process, how it knows relatable word and generate vector which can be plotted near by.
For example, how embedding model knows that Dog and Cat are coming under same category

=====================

During training, the embedding model is given millions of articles, books, and websites. It analyzes words by looking at their immediate neighbors.

Imagine the model reads these three sentences in its dataset:

"The veterinarian checked the health of the dog yesterday."

"The veterinarian checked the health of the cat yesterday."

"I fed my pet dog some kibble in the kitchen."

"I fed my pet cat some tuna in the kitchen."

Now, look at a completely different word, like "Microchip":
5. "The engineer soldered the microchip onto the circuit board."

The model notices that "dog" and "cat" constantly share identical neighbors like "veterinarian", "fed", "pet", and "health". Meanwhile, "microchip" hangs out with words like "soldered", "circuit", and "engineer".

Mathematically, because "dog" and "cat" share highly overlapping contexts, the training algorithm forces their vector coordinates closer together.


